      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\nAlthough \"maybe\" is the convention in the networking code, which I am using here as well, I personally don\u0027t like it very much. I just wanted to use the opportunity to explain why:\n\n\"maybe\" is imo descriptive of the implementation but not of its intent, which create a lot of ambiguity.\n\nHere the intent is not that the function returns early or may be a noop. Instead the intent is do some idempotent action.\n\nI feel that nuance is lost with \"maybe\". Instead I personally prefer name hints like \"ensureClatStarted\" that points better to idempotent semantics.",
      "parentUuid": "adbeb01d_0e9a7d71",
